2, Adair County&rsquo;s record runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, across 7 grids. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, February to March and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 35 years, the most of any pair. In 2025, July to August came in at 51% of normal on the middle, and so far in 2026 March to April sits at 50%. Grid 20579 and grid 20879 had their driest year in 1963 at 63% of normal.</p>"}
